WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

The star ratings collected here are the publications' own editorial judgements,
not ours. We record them as facts, count them, and link back to the original
review. Nothing in this notice claims ownership of any publication's rating,
review text, or headline, and nothing here restricts a publication's use of its
own material.

Individual facts — that a named publication awarded a named show four stars on
a given date — are not owned by anyone. What this repository contains is the
collation: the work of finding those reviews, reconciling how differently each
publication expresses a rating, and matching them to the right shows.

Ratings published on scales other than five stars are converted, and those
conversions are our editorial interpretation rather than the publication's
figure. The original is always displayed alongside so the distinction is
visible.


CORRECTIONS

If you are a publication and want a rating changed or removed, open an issue at
https://github.com/jamierd212/fringe-leaderboard/issues and it will be actioned.


This is a plain-English statement of intent, not legal advice. If anything here
becomes commercially significant, take proper advice — particularly on UK
database right, which is the part most likely to be relevant.
